    "narrative": "For the June 21 slate, the Austin Waves offense is primed for a high-output performance, anchored by the elite tier of **Kyle Tucker** (77.24) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.96). **Kyle Tucker** leads the charge against Young, benefiting significantly from a weak opposing starter (xERA 4.79) and a solid platoon advantage. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** provides excellent utility value; his score is buoyed by a favorable matchup against Martinez and a premium slot in the #2 hole, which maximizes his counting stat potential. **Andy Pages** (71.38) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.07) also clear the 70-point threshold, both enjoying prime positioning in their respective lineups against shaky arms, making them essential pivots if we are to manufacture the runs needed to climb the 5x5 standings.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the final spot in the middle infield/utility rotation. **Nasim Nunez** (49.49) fell just short of the starting lineup, despite his elite sprint speed and steal potential. While we covet his legs to bolster our standing in the scarce SB category, he is currently suppressed by a bottom-of-the-order assignment (#9) and a lower overall efficiency score compared to the aggressive plate appearances projected for **Curtis Mead** and **Jacob Wilson**. **Coby Mayo** was also considered, but with a sub-40 score (37.84) against Sheehan, he failed to meet the Waves' minimum efficiency floor, effectively benching himself in favor of higher-floor production.\n\nRisk management remains critical, particularly with **Jackson Merrill** (57.31) facing Eovaldi. While **Jackson Merrill** remains a high-upside start, Eovaldi represents an \"Elite Hold\" arm that actively threatens to diminish our stolen base opportunities. Similarly, while **Gunnar Henderson** (62.82) is a mandatory start due to his raw talent, the matchup against Sheehan is the toughest on our board (3.34 xERA). We will be monitoring the official lineups closely; 